  abstract = {In this article a new two-dimensional analytical model is presented, which explores the effects of longitudinal (aL) and transverse (aT) dispersivity on the transient and steady state length of a plume undergoing an instantaneous bimolecular reaction. A solute B is injected into a steady, uniform flow field in a homogeneous porous medium initially filled with a solute A. Mixing of the solutes occurs only through longitudinal and transversal dispersion and reaction between the solutes is assumed to occur where both solutes are simultaneously present.},
  langid = {english},
